Module: Decision Making (DM)
==============================
Description: This Module defines the process for making decisions regarding
the project, including acceptance of Contributions, allocation of
Contribution Shares, and other project-related matters. It also defines the
"Decision-Making Body."

Subsequent Phase (SP) -> Weighted Consensus (WC):
Decisions require the agreement of Participants whose combined Contribution
Shares represent a majority (more than 50%) of the total Contribution
Shares. This means that a Participant with a larger Contribution Share has
a greater influence on achieving consensus. If the required consensus is
not reached after a reasonable period of discussion (to be determined by
the Participants), the issue may be resolved by Majority Voting (MV), if
all Participants agree to switch to this voting method for the specific
issue at hand.

Interaction with Basic License: This Module replaces the generic provisions
regarding "Acceptance of Contributions and Participants" and "Contribution
Accounting and Share Allocation" in the Basic License. It also defines the
"Decision-Making Body."


Module: Commercialization (CM)
================================
Description: This Module defines the terms for commercial use of the
Program and the distribution of resulting revenues, if applicable.

Commercialization Allowed (CA) -> SESL Commerce (SC):
The Program is released under a specific commercial license derived from
SESL, the terms of which are defined in a separate document ("SESL Commerce
License").

Interaction with Basic License: This Module adds conditions to the "Grant
of Rights" section of the Basic License, specifically regarding commercial
use. It also defines how "Net Revenues" are calculated.


Module: Intellectual Property Management (IPM)
=================================================
Description: This Module defines the process for making decisions regarding
intellectual property rights related to the Program. It determines who has
the authority to choose or modify the specific IPP options defined in the
"Intellectual Property Protection" Module and how those decisions are made.

Delegated Decision to Participants (From the Start) (DP):
The Initiator delegates the decision on the IPP option(s) to the
Participants from the very beginning. The Participants will then choose one
of the options (A, B, C, or D) using the decision-making mechanism defined
in the "Decision Making" Module.

Interaction with Basic License: This Module determines who makes decisions
related to intellectual property rights, while the "Intellectual Property
Protection" Module defines what those options are. It supplements the
"Grant of Rights" section of the Basic License by specifying who has the
authority to grant specific rights related to intellectual property.
Transition to IPP Module: After the IPM Module determines who has the
authority to make decisions related to IP, the chosen IPP option(s) from the
"Intellectual Property Protection" Module then comes into effect.


Module: Intellectual Property Protection (IPP)
=================================================
Description: This Module defines the ownership and management of
intellectual property rights related to the Program.

Individual Ownership (Contribution-Based Copyright) (IO):
Each Participant retains the copyright to their own Contributions. Use,
modification, or distribution of a specific Contribution requires the
consent of the Participant who made that Contribution. The combination of
Contributions to create the Program as a whole is licensed under the terms
of the License Configuration.

Interaction with Basic License: This Module clarifies the ownership of
intellectual property rights related to the Program, supplementing the
"Grant of Rights" section of the Basic License.


